{{/*
family: softflowd
what: flow
transports: v9, ipfix
reference: softflowd(8) manual page (-i, -n, -v, -t)
verification: tested
ci: CI runs real softflowd with these options, flow v9 and IPFIX, and IPFIX over IPv6, replaying a capture file with -r in place of -i <INTERFACE> (a CI runner has no traffic to watch), so the interface choice itself isn't exercised.
*/}}
{{define "does"}}Runs softflowd on {{.Interface}} and exports the flows it sees to Woodshed as {{if eq .Transport "ipfix"}}IPFIX (RFC 7011){{else}}flow v9 (RFC 3954){{end}}.{{end}}

{{define "parts"}}
@@part command - Run softflowd (as root), or put the same options in your distribution's softflowd service settings
softflowd -i {{.Interface}} -n {{.HostPort}} -v {{if eq .Transport "ipfix"}}10{{else}}9{{end}} -t maxlife=60
@@part command - See what it's exporting
softflowctl statistics
{{end}}

{{define "notes"}}
{{if eq .Interface "<INTERFACE>"}}<INTERFACE> is the network interface to watch, as `ip link` names it.
{{end}}
-t maxlife=60 exports long-running flows every minute, so they show up during an incident rather than when they end.
softflowd sees only the traffic that passes the interface it watches.
{{end}}

{{define "check"}}Woodshed's Flows view lists this machine as an exporter within a minute or two; `softflowctl statistics` shows the flows it has sent.{{end}}
